/-!
# A full subcategory of the site of an algebraic stack (Stacks 07AK)

Let `S` be a scheme in a big fppf site `B`, let `p : 𝒳 ⥤ (Sch/S)` be a category fibred in
groupoids, and give `𝒳` one of the five sites of Stacks 06TP —
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.associatedTopology B S hS p τ`, the topology `𝒳` inherits from the
localization at `S` of a topology `τ` on the underlying category of schemes of `B`.

Let `𝒳' ⊆ 𝒳` be a *full* subcategory with the closure property of Stacks 07AK (1): if `x ⟶ x'`
is a morphism of `𝒳` lying over a smooth (respectively flat and locally finitely presented)
morphism of schemes and `x'` is an object of `𝒳'`, then so is `x`. Stacks 07AK declares a family
of morphisms of `𝒳'` to be a covering when it is a covering of `𝒳_τ`, which is
`P.ι.inheritedTopology` for the inclusion of the full subcategory (Stacks 06NV; the cartesianness
clause of Stacks 06NU is automatic for a fully faithful functor), and asserts that the inclusion
is then continuous and cocontinuous.

That is what this file proves, from
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isContinuous_ι_inheritedTopology` and
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isCocontinuous_ι_inheritedTopology`. The hypothesis those need is
that every covering sieve of the ambient site is refined by a covering family of morphisms lying
over morphisms with the closure property, and it is supplied here by transporting refinability
from the base twice, through
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.isRefinableBy_over` and
`CategoryTheory.Functor.isRefinableBy_inheritedTopology`.

The closure property is kept as a parameter `Q : MorphismProperty Scheme`, so that the two cases
of the source — `τ` étale with `Q = Smooth`, and `τ` fppf with
`Q = Flat ⊓ LocallyOfFinitePresentation` — are two instantiations rather than two proofs. For a
topology generated by a chosen collection of covering families, as all five of Stacks 03FF are,
the refinability hypothesis reduces to the statement that the members of a chosen covering family
satisfy `Q`; that is the `_of_members` form below.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isRefinableBy_associatedTopology`: every covering sieve of the
  associated site is refined by a covering family lying over `Q`-morphisms, as soon as the same
  holds on the base.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCocontinuous_ι_associatedTopology`: **Stacks 07AK**, continuity and
  cocontinuity of the inclusion of the full subcategory, for a general `τ` and `Q`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_members` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCocontinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_members`: the same with the
  refinability hypothesis replaced by the member condition on the chosen covering families
  generating `τ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isContinuous_ι_etaleTopology` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCocontinuous_ι_etaleTopology`: **Stacks 07AK** in the étale case,
  for an ambient topology generated by a chosen collection of étale covering families — which is
  what each of the four non-fppf topologies of Stacks 03FF is.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isContinuous_ι_fppfTopology` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCocontinuous_ι_fppfTopology`: **Stacks 07AK** in the fppf case,
  with every hypothesis beyond the two of the source discharged — `τ` is the chosen fppf topology
  `B.topology` and `Q` is `Flat ⊓ LocallyOfFinitePresentation`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07AK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07AK)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Smoothness of morphisms of schemes contains the identities. Mathlib has the instance
`Smooth (𝟙 X)` but not its packaging as `MorphismProperty.ContainsIdentities`, which is what the
étale case of Stacks 07AK consumes. -/
@[sga "1 II 1.3" "more general"]
instance smooth_containsIdentities : MorphismProperty.ContainsIdentities (@Smooth) :=
  ⟨fun _ ↦ inferInstance⟩

namespace Stack

universe u v w

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  {X : Type v} [Category.{w} X] (p : X ⥤ BigFppfOver B S hS)

/-- In a category fibred in groupoids every morphism is strongly cartesian over its own image
(Stacks 003V). -/
private lemma isStronglyCartesian_of_isFiberedInGroupoids
    (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {a b : X} (f : a ⟶ b) :
    p.IsStronglyCartesian (p.map f) f := by
  have : p.IsHomLift (p.map f) f := Functor.IsHomLift.map f
  exact hp.isStronglyCartesian_homLift (p.map f) f

variable (Q : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})

/-- **The refinement property of the site associated to a category fibred in groupoids.** If
every `τ`-covering sieve of the underlying category of schemes of `B` is refined by a covering
family of morphisms lying over `Q`-morphisms of schemes, then the same holds for every covering
sieve of `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.associatedTopology B S hS p τ`.

Two transports: first to the localization `(Sch/S)` of the base at `S`
(`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.isRefinableBy_over`), then up the structure functor
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.isRefinableBy_inheritedTopology`), where the cartesian lifts of a
`Q`-refinement downstairs provide the refinement upstairs. -/
theorem isRefinableBy_associatedTopology (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (τ : GrothendieckTopology B.Schemes)
    [MorphismProperty.ContainsIdentities Q] [MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderComposition Q]
    [MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderBaseChange Q]
    (hτ : ∀ ⦃V : B.Schemes⦄ (T : Sieve V), T ∈ τ V →
      τ.IsRefinableBy (Q.inverseImage B.inclusion) T)
    ⦃x : X⦄ (T : Sieve x) (hT : T ∈ associatedTopology B S hS p τ x) :
    (associatedTopology B S hS p τ).IsRefinableBy
      (((Q.inverseImage B.inclusion).inverseImage
        (BigFppfOver.forget B S hS)).inverseImage p) T := by
  have : p.IsFibered := hp.isFibered
  exact p.isRefinableBy_inheritedTopology
    (isStronglyCartesian_of_isFiberedInGroupoids B S hS p hp) _ _
    (τ.isRefinableBy_over (Q.inverseImage B.inclusion) (B.obj hS) hτ) T hT

/-- **Stacks 07AK, continuity.** Let `p : 𝒳 ⥤ (Sch/S)` be a category fibred in groupoids over the
big fppf category of a scheme `S` in `B`, endowed with the site of Stacks 06TP for a topology `τ`
on the underlying category of schemes of `B`, and let `P` cut out a full subcategory of `𝒳` closed
under the morphisms lying over `Q`-morphisms of schemes. If every `τ`-covering sieve is refined by
a covering family of `Q`-morphisms, the inclusion of the full subcategory is continuous for the
topology it inherits (Stacks 06NV). -/
theorem isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (τ : GrothendieckTopology B.Schemes) (P : ObjectProperty X)
    [MorphismProperty.ContainsIdentities Q] [MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderComposition Q]
    [MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderBaseChange Q]
    (hτ : ∀ ⦃V : B.Schemes⦄ (T : Sieve V), T ∈ τ V →
      τ.IsRefinableBy (Q.inverseImage B.inclusion) T)
    (hclose : ∀ ⦃x y : X⦄ (f : x ⟶ y), Q (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) → P y → P x) :
    P.ι.IsContinuous (P.ι.inheritedTopology (associatedTopology B S hS p τ))
      (associatedTopology B S hS p τ) := by
  have hcart : ∀ {a b : X} (f : a ⟶ b), p.IsStronglyCartesian (p.map f) f :=
    isStronglyCartesian_of_isFiberedInGroupoids B S hS p hp
  have : p.IsFibered := hp.isFibered
  have := p.isStableUnderBaseChange_inverseImage hcart
    ((Q.inverseImage B.inclusion).inverseImage (BigFppfOver.forget B S hS))
  exact ObjectProperty.isContinuous_ι_inheritedTopology
    (Q := ((Q.inverseImage B.inclusion).inverseImage
      (BigFppfOver.forget B S hS)).inverseImage p)
    (fun _ _ _ g f _ ↦ p.hasPullback_of_forall_isStronglyCartesian hcart g f)
    (fun _ _ f hf hy ↦ hclose f hf hy)
    (isRefinableBy_associatedTopology B S hS p Q hp τ hτ)

/-- **Stacks 07AK, cocontinuity.** Under the hypotheses of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology` the inclusion of the full subcategory
is also cocontinuous: a covering sieve of an object of the subcategory, refined by a covering
family of `Q`-morphisms, has all the sources of that family in the subcategory by closure. -/
theorem isCocontinuous_ι_associatedTopology (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (τ : GrothendieckTopology B.Schemes) (P : ObjectProperty X)
    [MorphismProperty.ContainsIdentities Q] [MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderComposition Q]
    [MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderBaseChange Q]
    (hτ : ∀ ⦃V : B.Schemes⦄ (T : Sieve V), T ∈ τ V →
      τ.IsRefinableBy (Q.inverseImage B.inclusion) T)
    (hclose : ∀ ⦃x y : X⦄ (f : x ⟶ y), Q (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) → P y → P x) :
    P.ι.IsCocontinuous (P.ι.inheritedTopology (associatedTopology B S hS p τ))
      (associatedTopology B S hS p τ) :=
  ObjectProperty.isCocontinuous_ι_inheritedTopology
    (fun _ _ f hf hy ↦ hclose f hf hy)
    (isRefinableBy_associatedTopology B S hS p Q hp τ hτ)

/-! ### Topologies given by a chosen collection of covering families -/

section OfMembers

variable (K : Precoverage B.Schemes)
  [MorphismProperty.ContainsIdentities Q] [MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderComposition Q]
  [MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderBaseChange Q]
  (hK : ∀ ⦃V : B.Schemes⦄ (R : Presieve V), R ∈ K V →
    ∀ ⦃W : B.Schemes⦄ (g : W ⟶ V), R g → Q (B.inclusion.map g))

include hK

/-- For a topology on the underlying category of schemes generated by a chosen collection of
covering families — as all five topologies of Stacks 03FF are — refinability is the statement
that the members of a chosen covering family satisfy `Q`. -/
theorem isRefinableBy_toGrothendieck_of_members ⦃V : B.Schemes⦄ (T : Sieve V)
    (hT : T ∈ K.toGrothendieck V) :
    K.toGrothendieck.IsRefinableBy (Q.inverseImage B.inclusion) T :=
  Precoverage.isRefinableBy_of_members (Q := Q.inverseImage B.inclusion)
    (fun _ _ _ _ _ _ ↦ inferInstance) (fun _ R hR _ g hg ↦ hK R hR g hg) T hT

/-- **Stacks 07AK, continuity**, for an ambient topology generated by a chosen collection of
covering families whose members satisfy `Q`. -/
theorem isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_members (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (P : ObjectProperty X)
    (hclose : ∀ ⦃x y : X⦄ (f : x ⟶ y), Q (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) → P y → P x) :
    P.ι.IsContinuous (P.ι.inheritedTopology (associatedTopology B S hS p K.toGrothendieck))
      (associatedTopology B S hS p K.toGrothendieck) :=
  isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology B S hS p Q hp _ P
    (isRefinableBy_toGrothendieck_of_members B Q K hK) hclose

/-- **Stacks 07AK, cocontinuity**, for an ambient topology generated by a chosen collection of
covering families whose members satisfy `Q`. -/
theorem isCocontinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_members (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (P : ObjectProperty X)
    (hclose : ∀ ⦃x y : X⦄ (f : x ⟶ y), Q (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) → P y → P x) :
    P.ι.IsCocontinuous (P.ι.inheritedTopology (associatedTopology B S hS p K.toGrothendieck))
      (associatedTopology B S hS p K.toGrothendieck) :=
  isCocontinuous_ι_associatedTopology B S hS p Q hp _ P
    (isRefinableBy_toGrothendieck_of_members B Q K hK) hclose

end OfMembers

/-! ### The fppf case -/

/-- Every member of a chosen covering family of a big fppf site is flat and locally of finite
presentation: the chosen families are fppf coverings (Stacks 021R), and membership in Mathlib's
fppf precoverage is by definition joint surjectivity together with these two properties of each
member. -/
theorem flat_and_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_mem_precoverage ⦃V : B.Schemes⦄
    (R : Presieve V) (hR : R ∈ B.precoverage V) ⦃W : B.Schemes⦄ (g : W ⟶ V) (hg : R g) :
    Flat (B.inclusion.map g) ∧ LocallyOfFinitePresentation (B.inclusion.map g) := by
  obtain ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩ := hR
  exact (B.isFppfCovering_of_isCovering hE).2 (Presieve.map_map hg)

/-- Being flat and locally of finite presentation is stable under identities, composition and
base change, hence usable as the closure property of Stacks 07AK in the fppf case. -/
lemma flat_and_locallyOfFinitePresentation_instances :
    MorphismProperty.ContainsIdentities
        ((@Flat : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) ⊓ @LocallyOfFinitePresentation) ∧
      MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderComposition
        ((@Flat : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) ⊓ @LocallyOfFinitePresentation) ∧
      MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderBaseChange
        ((@Flat : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) ⊓ @LocallyOfFinitePresentation) :=
  ⟨⟨fun _ ↦ ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩⟩,
    MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderComposition.inf, MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderBaseChange.inf⟩

/-- Being flat and locally of finite presentation is stable under identities, composition and
base change, hence usable as the closure property of Stacks 07AK in the fppf case. -/
private alias flatLfp_instances := flat_and_locallyOfFinitePresentation_instances

/-- **Continuity of the inclusion in Stacks 07AK, fppf case.** A full subcategory of a category
fibred in groupoids over the big fppf category of `S`, closed under the morphisms lying over a
flat, locally finitely presented morphism of schemes, includes continuously into the fppf site of
Stacks 06TP. -/
theorem isContinuous_ι_fppfTopology (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (P : ObjectProperty X)
    (hclose : ∀ ⦃x y : X⦄ (f : x ⟶ y), Flat (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) →
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) → P y → P x) :
    P.ι.IsContinuous (P.ι.inheritedTopology (associatedTopology B S hS p B.topology))
      (associatedTopology B S hS p B.topology) := by
  obtain ⟨h₁, h₂, h₃⟩ := flatLfp_instances.{u}
  exact isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_members B S hS p
    ((@Flat : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) ⊓ @LocallyOfFinitePresentation) B.precoverage
    (flat_and_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_mem_precoverage B) hp P
    fun _ _ f hf ↦ hclose f hf.1 hf.2

/-- **Cocontinuity of the inclusion in Stacks 07AK, fppf case.** The same inclusion is
cocontinuous. -/
theorem isCocontinuous_ι_fppfTopology (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (P : ObjectProperty X)
    (hclose : ∀ ⦃x y : X⦄ (f : x ⟶ y), Flat (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) →
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) → P y → P x) :
    P.ι.IsCocontinuous (P.ι.inheritedTopology (associatedTopology B S hS p B.topology))
      (associatedTopology B S hS p B.topology) := by
  obtain ⟨h₁, h₂, h₃⟩ := flatLfp_instances.{u}
  exact isCocontinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_members B S hS p
    ((@Flat : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) ⊓ @LocallyOfFinitePresentation) B.precoverage
    (flat_and_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_mem_precoverage B) hp P
    fun _ _ f hf ↦ hclose f hf.1 hf.2

/-! ### The étale case -/

section Etale

variable (K : Precoverage B.Schemes)
  (hK : ∀ ⦃V : B.Schemes⦄ (R : Presieve V), R ∈ K V →
    R.map B.inclusion ∈ Scheme.etalePrecoverage (B.inclusion.obj V))

include hK

/-- Every member of a covering family of a precoverage of `B.Schemes` whose image is an étale
covering family of schemes is smooth: it is étale, and an étale morphism is smooth. This is the
member condition of `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_members` for
`Q = Smooth` and any of the étale precoverages of Stacks 03FF. -/
theorem smooth_of_mem_of_map_mem_etalePrecoverage ⦃V : B.Schemes⦄ (R : Presieve V)
    (hR : R ∈ K V) ⦃W : B.Schemes⦄ (g : W ⟶ V) (hg : R g) : Smooth (B.inclusion.map g) := by
  have : Etale (B.inclusion.map g) := (hK R hR).2 (Presieve.map_map hg)
  infer_instance

/-- **Stacks 07AK, continuity, étale case.** A full subcategory of a category fibred in groupoids
over the big fppf category of `S`, closed under the morphisms lying over a smooth morphism of
schemes, includes continuously into the étale site of Stacks 06TP — for any of the étale
precoverages of Stacks 03FF, i.e. any chosen collection of étale covering families. -/
theorem isContinuous_ι_etaleTopology (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (P : ObjectProperty X)
    (hclose : ∀ ⦃x y : X⦄ (f : x ⟶ y), Smooth (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) → P y → P x) :
    P.ι.IsContinuous (P.ι.inheritedTopology (associatedTopology B S hS p K.toGrothendieck))
      (associatedTopology B S hS p K.toGrothendieck) :=
  isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_members B S hS p (@Smooth) K
    (smooth_of_mem_of_map_mem_etalePrecoverage B K hK) hp P hclose

/-- **Stacks 07AK, cocontinuity, étale case.** The same inclusion is cocontinuous. -/
theorem isCocontinuous_ι_etaleTopology (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (P : ObjectProperty X)
    (hclose : ∀ ⦃x y : X⦄ (f : x ⟶ y), Smooth (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) → P y → P x) :
    P.ι.IsCocontinuous (P.ι.inheritedTopology (associatedTopology B S hS p K.toGrothendieck))
      (associatedTopology B S hS p K.toGrothendieck) :=
  isCocontinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_members B S hS p (@Smooth) K
    (smooth_of_mem_of_map_mem_etalePrecoverage B K hK) hp P hclose

end Etale

end Stack

end AlgebraicGeometry

